\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> burette is zero. The volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution left in the burette after the end point is.......&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math>. (nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "189aaf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f546d"}, {"id": "c60f52", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f546e"}, {"id": "177716", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f546f"}, {"id": "f527e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5470"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5471", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477a"], "concepts": ["6162fb9c6ed13040ec850f09"], "question": {"text": "In alkaline medium, the reduction of permanganate anion involves a gain of ____________ electrons.&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "079da0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5472"}, {"id": "4fafb3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5473"}, {"id": "a886e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5474"}, {"id": "0c1983", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5475"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5476", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e5676a499d1e49588f8f0a"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9258"], "question": {"text": "Dichromate ion is treated with base, the oxidation number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> in the product formed is&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</u>"}, "options": [{"id": "798eed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5477"}, {"id": "5ed70f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5478"}, {"id": "61018c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5479"}, {"id": "f2f0a5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f48"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ec"], "question": {"text": "<p>See the following chemical reaction:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>XH</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>YCr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ZH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The sum of X, Y and Z is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2325cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547c"}, {"id": "c5076c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547d"}, {"id": "557d8c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547e"}, {"id": "ed1f94", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f547f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5480", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477a"], "concepts": ["61ab792e6fe44bfe0fe4ac68"], "question": {"text": "The volume, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math>, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><msub><mi>MK</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>, solution required to react with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>288</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of ferrous oxalate in acidic&nbsp;medium is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math> (Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><msup><mi>gmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "068f8d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5481"}, {"id": "1bbed0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5482"}, {"id": "e705e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5483"}, {"id": "7cdb46", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5484"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5485", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e5676a499d1e49588f8f0a"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ee6"], "question": {"text": "In mildly alkaline medium, thiosulphate ion is oxidized by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#34;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></math>. The oxidation state of sulphur in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#34;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></math> is_"}, "options": [{"id": "2e9206", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5486"}, {"id": "729d79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5487"}, {"id": "ea71ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5488"}, {"id": "5f3f45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5489"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f48"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f23"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>bC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>cH</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>xMn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>yCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>zH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br />If the above equation is balanced with integer coefficients, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>&nbsp;is _______ . (Round off to the Nearest Integer)."}, "options": [{"id": "4f2c81", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548b"}, {"id": "242fbb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548c"}, {"id": "a49257", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548d"}, {"id": "8568e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f548f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e567fd499d1e49588fa04a"], "concepts": ["6162fb9c6ed13040ec850ef8"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>166</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> sample of an organic compound was digested with conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and then distilled with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math>. The ammonia gas evolved was passed through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>. The used acid required <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaOH</mi></math> for complete neutralization. The mass percentage of nitrogen in the organic compound is"}, "options": [{"id": "241f02", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5490"}, {"id": "1d0d41", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5491"}, {"id": "8c29b7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5492"}, {"id": "8036be", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5493"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5494", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477a"], "concepts": ["63d250d8c55fda0b9ff1162a"], "question": {"text": "Some $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ gas was kept in a sealed container at a pressure of 1 atm and at 273 K . This entire amount of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ gas was later passed through an aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$. The excess unreacted $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$ was later neutralized with 0.1 M of 40 mL HCl . If the volume of the sealed container of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ was $x$, then $x$ is ________ $\\mathrm{cm}^3$ (nearest integer). \n[Given : The entire amount of $\\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$ reacted with exactly half the initial amount of $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$ present in the aqueous solution.]"}, "options": [{"id": "07ecba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5495"}, {"id": "7a6015", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5496"}, {"id": "75e62f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5497"}, {"id": "6b181d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5498"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f5499", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f48"], "concepts": ["6162fb996ed13040ec850d00"], "question": {"text": "<p>The reaction of sulphur in alkaline medium is given below:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>OH</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo></msubsup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></msub></math></p><p>The values of &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&#39; is______&nbsp;(Integer answer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5a1502", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549a"}, {"id": "4c4b9e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549b"}, {"id": "729c85", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549c"}, {"id": "53708d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e567fd499d1e49588fa04a"], "concepts": ["6162fb9c6ed13040ec850ef8"], "question": {"text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> solution containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> impure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> reacts completely with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>316</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> in acid solution. The purity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math>) is______ &nbsp;(mol. wt. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>34</mn></math>; mol. wt. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>158</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "25436c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f549f"}, {"id": "3d352b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f54a0"}, {"id": "f911bb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f54a1"}, {"id": "28612e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f54a2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef9c677dc36a88f54a3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e11c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4732"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> hypo solution is used for the titration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of copper sulphate solution, in the presence of excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KI</mi></math> using starch as an indicator. The molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;(nearest integer)</p><p>Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8212;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "76a795", "text": "", "isC